config BR2_PACKAGE_PORTSMOKE_SM64
    bool "SM64 native movement prototype .lilpck"
    depends on BR2_INSTALL_LIBSTDCPP
    depends on BR2_mipsel
    depends on BR2_TOOLCHAIN_HAS_THREADS
    select BR2_PACKAGE_HOST_PYTHON3
    select BR2_PACKAGE_SDL2
    select BR2_PACKAGE_WEBP
    help
      Independent SM64 development app: extract validated US ROM assets on
      the device, without Python, a compiler, a GPU, or bundled game data.
      Produces a bundled .lilpck in BINARIES_DIR, not a shared .peng.
      Includes a native ROM-derived Bob-omb Battlefield scene, a pinned MIT
      static CPU rasterizer, original Mario model/animations, basic movement,
      collision and jump handling. Includes a native WebP progress screen.
      Successful extraction deletes only the app's verified original ROM copy.
      Checked private caches are reused on future launches. User data and
      saves are created inside the installed independent app, never bundled.
      There is no system GL/GPU or N64 emulator. This is not the complete game;
      enemies, stars, other levels, advanced actions and audio are absent.
      This option is intentionally off by default.

comment "SM64 BYO-Data tools need a C++ toolchain"
    depends on !BR2_INSTALL_LIBSTDCPP
